+/*
+ * SM-T970 cameras, kernel step K1 (work/gps_camera_scope/SCOPE.md §2.4): power a sensor, read its ID over the CCI, receive
+ * its MIPI CSI-2 stream through a CSIPHY and CSID-lite0, and write one RAW frame to memory through IFE-lite0's RDI write
+ * master. USB commands only, nothing runs at boot (default off). Every command runs on its own thread; `cam` shows the result.
+ *
+ *   cam                         status of the last run (stage, IDs, receive counters, frame measure, AE)
+ *   cam id [front|rear|wide|all]                C1: power, CCI, chip ID (SMIA 0x0000..0x0003), power off
+ *   cam stream [sensor]                         C2a: mode_select on the power-on defaults, frame_count at 100 / 400 ms
+ *   cam rx [sensor] [lanes=N] [settle=N]        C3a: CSIPHY + CSID-lite0 receive for 300 ms, packet / ECC / CRC counters
+ *   cam frame [sensor] [lines=N] [ae] [exp=N] [gain=N] [target=N] [lanes=N] [settle=N] [pa=0x..]
+ *                               C4 (+C4b with `ae`): one RAW frame, lines N around the centre (default 480, 0 = whole frame),
+ *                               measured, 64x48 thumbnail kept; the frame stays in the buffer for `cam save`
+ *   cam thumb [row]             8 thumbnail rows from row (0..47): "tNN <128 hex>" (one Bayer site, 8-bit MSBs)
+ *   cam save [grbg|gbrg]        the last frame as a half-resolution colour PPM (2x2 Bayer quads, black 16, grey world,
+ *                               gamma 2) at /private/var/mobile/Media/DCIM/pong-cam.ppm, fetched with
+ *                               scripts/ios_usb_fileget.py; GBRG by default (JeyKul gts7xl-mainline 0038, front and wide)
+ * Sensors (ref/rui-gts7xlwifi-1111/docs/camera-notes.md:39-63, JeyKul 0033/0035): front S5K4HA CCI0 m1 0x2d CSIPHY 3 lanes
+ * 0..3; rear S5K3M5 CCI0 m0 0x2d CSIPHY 0 lanes reversed (assign 0x0123); wide S5K5E9 CCI1 m0 0x10 CSIPHY 2 two lanes.
+ * Only the front path has produced frames (rui, on the device, 11-11); rear and wide streams run on the sensors' power-on
+ * defaults here, untried.
+ *
+ * Frame buffer: pil_cdsp_region 0x8e300000 (26 MiB, no CDSP is started on this port), only when none of its pages is XNU
+ * RAM (else `cam frame` stops with c4 -1 det -2); pa= overrides it.
+ * The apps SMMU routes the IFE streams (0x800/0x801/0x840/0x841, mask 0x400) to a bypass bank (a bypass-emulation bank already
+ * in use is shared) for the frame only, then restores what it found.
+ *
+ * Port of ref/rui-gts7xlwifi-1111/package/T970Camera.cpp (UniXNU-gts7xlwifi, BSD-2-Clause-Patent, 11-11) stages C1, C2a,
+ * C3a, C4, C4b: same registers, values and order (camcc-sm8250.c, i2c-qcom-cci.c, camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c lane_regs_sm8250,
+ * cam_ife_csid_lite480.h, camss-vfe-480.c, camss-csid-gen2.c). Status words keep rui's t970_camera[] layout so his notes
+ * apply: [0] stage (negative = failed there), [1] detail, [2] GDSCR, [3] CCI version, [4..6] ID per sensor (0 not tried, -1
+ * NACK, -2 timeout, -3 CCI error), [7] last CCI IRQ, [8] ms, [9..11] C2a, [12..27] C3a, [28..39] C4. Changes: C instead of
+ * IOKit (ml_io_map windows mapped once), any sensor's CSIPHY selectable, the crop is the default, the frame can be saved.
+ */
+
